<article class="env-lemma" id="0542">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0542">Lemma <span data-tag="0542">5.19.10</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Noetherian sober topological space. Let $E \subset X$ be a subset of $X$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $E$ is constructible and stable under specialization, then $E$ is closed. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $E$ is constructible and stable under generalization, then $E$ is open. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $E$ be constructible and stable under generalization. Let $Y \subset X$ be an irreducible closed subset with generic point $\xi \in Y$. If $E \cap Y$ is nonempty, then it contains $\xi $ (by stability under generalization) and hence is dense in $Y$, hence it contains a nonempty open of $Y$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/053Z" data-tag="053Z">5.16.3</a>. Thus $E$ is open by Lemma <a href="/tag/0541" data-tag="0541">5.16.5</a>. This proves (2). To prove (1) apply (2) to the complement of $E$ in $X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>